Description: Specify mixed models using familiar 'ASReml' or 'brms'-style
    formula syntax and estimate them via 'INLA' or 'brms' ('Stan'). Returns
    results in formats compatible with the standard R modelling ecosystem
    including 'summary()', 'emmeans' and 'marginaleffects'.
    The package translates 'ASReml'-style formulas (fixed, random, residual)
    to backend-specific code ('INLA' or 'brms') using an indexing approach,
    scales to large agricultural datasets by accumulating exact per-cell
    sufficient statistics for the replicated designs that admit them (the
    benchmark record is in inst/validation), and compares the same model
    across engines with triangulate(), a diagnostic on a gated overlap rather
    than a validation contract. Supports Gaussian, binomial, Poisson,
    negative binomial, gamma, and beta families, and selected structured
    covariance models: diagonal and unstructured genotype-by-environment
    variances, per-level residual variances, known-covariance genomic and
    pedigree models, separable AR1 spatial fields on 'INLA', and univariate
    P-splines. Structures outside this set raise typed refusals naming the
    nearest implemented alternative.
